    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0729" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/9–953: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aldrich</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-09-09T19:00:00+01:00">September 9,
                            1953—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1027. Department pass USUN New York 11. Foreign Office still actively studying
                    question Chinese representation United Nations and attempting find formula which
                    will (1) enable it ward off opposition PQ s, (2) avoid embarrassment to
                    Department, (3) deep public airing United States-United Kingdom differences out
                    of United Nations forum, and (4) afford flexibility in dealing with Communists.
                    Foreign Office states United States formula described Department telegrams 1235
                    and 1272 presents difficulties in that question of credentials must be taken up
                    before fixing of closing date for General Assembly, and moratorium for duration
                    will certainly render government subject attack and may harden Communist
                    attitude toward political conference.</p>
                <p>Embassy given to understand, however, in absence something better, United Kingdom
                    likely concur in formula similar to that suggested reference telegrams.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aldrich</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
